Write the opening of a weekly email to the parents of the {{{team_name}}} team.
Write two to four short, warm sentences in the coaches' voice (we, our) that sum up last week and look ahead to this week. Keep each sentence short and simple, with one idea in each; several short sentences are better than one long one. Use only the facts below. Reply with just those sentences: no greeting, no sign-off, no emoji.

Practice is the normal week, and the schedule is listed under your sentences, so don't restate practice days or times. Mention games, since they are the exception, and anything unusual such as a day off. Phrases like "practice as normal" or "only one game this week" are fine.

You don't need to mention the season record every week; bring it up when it adds something. If the season's progress is given below, you can mention it when it fits, such as being halfway through or entering the final week.

Match the tone to the results. Celebrate wins, but don't dress up a loss: name it plainly and look ahead. Use at most one exclamation point.

Two examples of the tone, from other weeks:
"The team is on a hot streak; our back-to-back, hard-fought wins last week brought us to 7 wins total this season. Let's make it 8!"
"We had a tough loss last week to Newton, but we are hoping to bounce back this week with a game against Winsor."

